# Read by `npm pack` and by `pnpm deploy`, which is how the desktop app builds
# its server bundle (`pnpm bundle:server`). Both walk THIS package directory and
# never read the repo-root .gitignore, so a path being git-ignored says nothing
# about whether it gets copied.
#
# Without this file, `pnpm dist` copies the dev data directory — a quarter
# gigabyte of PGlite files plus every scan capture — into
# packages/desktop/.server-bundle on every build, and the pruner then walks it.
# Only .server-bundle/dist and .server-bundle/node_modules are packaged
# (see electron-builder.yml extraResources), so none of this is wanted there.
.poke-sort*
.turbo/
eval/
*.traineddata
